---
description: After changing application code, check that critical user journeys still work in a real browser
alwaysApply: true
---

When you change application code (not only docs, comments or tests), check the app still works before you say you're done:

1. Make sure the dev server is running.
2. Run `npx stillworks run --no-promo` in the terminal. It runs signup, login, checkout and the other journeys in `journeys.config.ts` in a real browser.
3. If it fails, read `verify-report/REPORT.md` and the screenshot it points to. Fix the root cause, starting from the failed requests and console errors.
   - Don't change files unrelated to the failure.
   - Don't edit `journeys.config.ts` to make a check pass.
4. Run it again until every journey passes (at most 3 tries), then tell me what broke and what you changed.
